| 11..34 | H5X sets (`artifacts.lua`) | DLL only — 11 Haven: `ArtfsetHaven.cpp`, 12 Sylvan: `ArtfsetPreserve.cpp`, 13 Inferno: `ArtfsetInferno.cpp`, 14 Necropolis: `ArtfsetNecro.cpp`, 15 Academy: `ArtfsetAcademy.cpp`, 16 Dungeon: `ArtfsetDungeon.cpp`, 17 Dwarven: `ArtfsetDwarven.cpp`, 18 Orcs: `ArtfsetOrcs.cpp` | |

`0x004D8D7F` is the generic call inside `0x004D8D60`.

The commented-out `ArtfsetRepoint_init` patches the immediate byte of each `push`. Its entry `0x008CE933` (Ogres 2*) points at the opcode instead: the immediate is at `0x008CE934`.

## Expansion to 40 sets (`ArtfsetExpand.cpp`)

| Patch | Effect |
|---|---|
| `PATCH_BYTE 0x00B58C99`, `0x00B5910D` = 40 | Constructors create 40 counts |
| `PATCH_BYTE 0x00B515ED` = 40 | The equip handler builds 40 counts |
| `PATCH_BYTE 0x00B5164B` = 40 | The equip handler counts set IDs up to 40 |
| `PATCH_HOOK 0x00B5AD70` (6) → `ArtifactSetCountFork` | Bounds-checked getter: returns 0 when `set_id` is outside the vector, so a 10-entry vector (from an older save, until the next equip change) is never read past its end |

Before this, only the getter's bound was raised (`0x00B5AD7A`). Counts for IDs > 10 were never written, and the getter read past the 10-entry vector.

### Equip hook (`ArtfsetExpand.cpp`)

`func_CheckArtifactPassiveEffects` (`0x00B5A410`, `this` = CHero = IHero − 0x1C, args (?, artifact DB record, equipped flag)) runs after every equip / unequip — the equip handler `FUN_00b543d0` and `0x00B574FA` / `0x00B5754E` call `func_UpdateArtifactSetCounts` (set counts) first. It applies the artifact's stats (`FUN_00b53a50`), its spells (`func_AddArtifactSpells` equip: `FUN_00CA6930` collects the artifact's spells, each pushed to the spellbook `[CHero+0x1E0]` with the artifact as handle; `func_RemoveArtifactSpells` unequip removes them unless another artifact gives them — Band of the Conjurer works this way), then the spellbook refresh `func_RefreshHeroSpellbook` at `0x00B5A4AA`, which `ArtfsetExpand.cpp` replaces (`PATCH_CALL`) to run the set equip effects first. Permanent learning: `IHero +0xE8` (`learn_spell`, `0x00B54720` → `func_HeroLearnSpell(spell, 0, flag)`).

